{"ts": 1791255667.8813288, "type": "step", "step": 23, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "What an environment is"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 22, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.37516055148468447, "pomdp": 0.35853496713560185, "pass_k": 0.27998147170370613}, "p_perf": {"attention": 1.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8030104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.34481971324228816, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255669.567893, "type": "step", "step": 24, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Next step: turn the readings into a build plan.\n\nFor your build, you need two deliverables:\n1) an explicit environment definition: state, observations, actions, and dynamics\n2) evaluation across at least 3 seeds, using pass^k\n\nHere\u2019s the useful way to structure your work:\n- State: what is fully true in the environment, even if the agent can\u2019t see it?\n- Observation: what does the agent actually get to see?\n- Action: what choices can the agent make?\n- Dynamics: how does the state change after an action?\n- Evaluation: run the same setup on 3 seeds and report whether it succeeds on all runs (pass^k), not just any run\n\nCan you draft a 4-bullet environment definition for your project? If you paste it here, I\u2019ll help you tighten it into build-ready wording.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-environments"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now", "t": 24, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.37516055148468447, "pomdp": 0.44753736883341116, "pass_k": 0.27998147170370613}, "p_perf": {"attention": 1.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8030104796182297, "motivation": 0.8330753570864192, "reliance": 0.3648197132422882, "persistence": 0.48938443592806424, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3136352668677162, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2892105949863653, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
